{
  "id": "23054_inin",
  "headword": "{委任|いにん}",
  "reading": "いにん",
  "romaji": "inin",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, verb-suru",
  "gloss": "delegation; mandate; entrusting",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "delegation; entrusting; mandate; authorization",
      "explanation": "The act of entrusting someone with authority, responsibility, or a task. Commonly used in legal and business contexts for formal delegation of powers."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "23054_inin_ex1",
      "japanese": "{権限|けんげん}を{委任|いにん}する。",
      "english": "To delegate authority.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23054_inin_ex2",
      "japanese": "{弁護士|べんごし}に{手続|てつづ}きを{委任|いにん}した。",
      "english": "I entrusted the procedures to a lawyer.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23054_inin_ex3",
      "japanese": "{総会|そうかい}に{出席|しゅっせき}できない{場合|ばあい}は、{委任状|いにんじょう}を{提出|ていしゅつ}してください。",
      "english": "If you cannot attend the general meeting, please submit a proxy form.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal word composed of {委|い} (entrust) + {任|にん} (responsibility/duty). Primarily used in legal, business, and administrative contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {委任|いにん}する: to delegate, to entrust\n- {委任状|いにんじょう}: letter of proxy, power of attorney\n- {委任|いにん}{契約|けいやく}: mandate contract\n- {権限|けんげん}を{委任|いにん}する: to delegate authority\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {委託|いたく}: consignment, outsourcing — entrusting a specific task or item to another party; often commercial\n- {任命|にんめい}: appointment — formally assigning someone to a position\n- {代理|だいり}: proxy, representation — acting on behalf of someone else\n- {託|たく}す: to entrust — a more general and literary verb",
